# DEFECT y_fill_bias (tests/v6n/DEFECTS.md), texel symptom: render/native/gl/nxgl.c moves all geometry up by
# 1/256 px (NXGL_Y_FILL_BIAS), which also moves every interpolated attribute. Full-target quad, v running 1 -> 0
# from top to bottom, POINT sampling of a 16x16 texture: every pixel centre lands exactly on a texel boundary
# (the un-offset D3D9 full-screen quad). Nine selects texel row 15 - y; the biased attribute selects 14 - y.
# The coverage symptom is checked against the exact D3D9 rule by render/verify/rastercheck.py.
size 16 16
rt A8R8G8B8
ds NONE
clear 1 0xff000000 1.0 0
rs CULLMODE CULL_NONE
tex 0 A8R8G8B8 16 16 1 hash 41
samp 0 MINFILTER TEXF_POINT
samp 0 MAGFILTER TEXF_POINT
tss 0 COLOROP TOP_SELECTARG1
tss 0 COLORARG1 TA_TEXTURE
tss 0 ALPHAOP TOP_SELECTARG1
tss 0 ALPHAARG1 TA_TEXTURE
mode rhw
v 0 0 0.5 1 0xffffffff 0 0.03125 1
v 16 0 0.5 1 0xffffffff 0 1.03125 1
v 0 16 0.5 1 0xffffffff 0 0.03125 0
v 16 0 0.5 1 0xffffffff 0 1.03125 1
v 16 16 0.5 1 0xffffffff 0 1.03125 0
v 0 16 0.5 1 0xffffffff 0 0.03125 0
draw TRIANGLELIST 2
